# Private keys never belong in this public repository, in any form git can read.
# The patterns match anywhere in the tree and after any chezmoi prefix, because
# `chezmoi add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519` would write private_dot_ssh/private_id_ed25519.
#
# This only stops `git add .` and friends; `git add -f` and a file that is
# already tracked get past it. The detect-private-key and no-age-identity
# pre-commit hooks read the content instead, and catch a key under any name.
#
# An encrypted_*.age copy ends in .age and is not matched: ciphertext is how
# this repository keeps secrets. See docs/secrets.md.

# ssh private keys under their default names; the .pub files are not matched
*id_rsa
*id_dsa
*id_ecdsa
*id_ecdsa_sk
*id_ed25519
*id_ed25519_sk
*id_xmss

# other private key and certificate bundle formats
*.pem
*.ppk
*.p12
*.pfx

# the chezmoi age identity, which decrypts every .age file here
**/chezmoi/*key.txt
